  "event_note": "Named events per Pacific day. pageview is a plain page read; the other names are the record's return markers \u2014 changed-read (a /changed check-back; since Oct 19, 2026 the format-specific names changed-read-json and changed-read-atom are recorded when the response's format is known), utility-read (a published utility used), receipt-check (a receipt looked up), notes-read and guestbook-view (the visitors' book read as counts and page), data-read (a /data file read), counts-read (the public counts payload read), ledger-read (the public ledger file read). An event is a request to a path, nothing more.",
  "file_days": null,
  "file_note": "Fetches of the canonical agent-interest files per Pacific day \u2014 the discovery set (robots.txt, llms.txt, sitemap, security.txt, the agent card, the agent skills) and the instruction-file probes (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md). A fetch is a request, not evidence of agent interest: measured experience is that these hits are likelier scanners and audit tools. The series exists so a second crawler pass is visible as a pass.",
